@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] review-bot-handle-list
An `r?` line starts with at most three spaces and whitespace after `r?`; its handle list consists
of consecutive whitespace-separated GitHub user mentions or bare `cc`, case-insensitively, and ends
at the first other token. Only `cc` in that list requests a contract review; quotes, fenced or
indented code, and HTML comments never introduce requests, including across hidden line breaks.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:architecture] review-bot-output
The review bot emits `pull-request-number` only for a human's eligible request and requests no
review when that output is empty.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] review-bot-dispatch
When a review workflow is configured, the bot dispatches it on the eligible PR's head branch only
after verifying requester access and PR eligibility, passing the PR number and original request
run ID. Without that configuration, the detector makes no GitHub changes.
